# Copy to .env and fill in — or let the application do it: pasting a key into
# the model dialog's "api key" field writes this file. The engine loads it as its
# project env layer (inherited environment first, then this file), so a value
# exported in the shell wins. This is the ONLY credential the harness reads —
# never use DEEPSEEK_API_KEY: the shipped DeepSeek routes are mounted off, and
# the provider this application mounts reads AI_API_KEY exclusively.
AI_API_KEY=

# The model. With nothing else set, the harness runs OpenRouter's DeepSeek
# (deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash at https://openrouter.ai/api/v1) on AI_API_KEY.
# To run another model, name it here — no source change, no restart of setup:
# AI_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.7-plus
# AI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# The working context compaction keeps the conversation within (tokens):
# AI_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
# Output tokens one response may use (default 2000). Some providers (Groq is
# one) reject a request above their own per-model output ceiling even though
# it is well under the context window above — raise this only if your route
# allows more:
# AI_MAX_TOKENS=2000
#
# A workspace's .harness/models.json `active` route (what the application's
# model dialog writes) wins over these. The budget caps and the committee bench
# are declared in App/dsh-plugins/hackathon-harness-preset/cordis.yml and
# overridden from a profile patch — never from here.
